!Sample_label_protocol_ch1	"Biotin-labeled cRNA samples for hybridization were prepared according to Illumina's recommended sample labeling procedure: 750 ng of total RNA was used for cDNA synthesis, followed by an amplification/labeling step (in vitro transcription) to synthesize biotin-labeled cRNA using the Illumina TotalPrep RNA Amplification kit (Ambion, Inc., Austin, TX). cRNA concentrations were determined using a spectrophotometer (Nanodrop, ND-1000)."	"Biotin-labeled cRNA samples for hybridization were prepared according to Illumina's recommended sample labeling procedure: 750 ng of total RNA was used for cDNA synthesis, followed by an amplification/labeling step (in vitro transcription) to synthesize biotin-labeled cRNA using the Illumina TotalPrep RNA Amplification kit (Ambion, Inc., Austin, TX). cRNA concentrations were determined using a spectrophotometer (Nanodrop, ND-1000)."	"Biotin-labeled cRNA samples for hybridization were prepared according to Illumina's recommended sample labeling procedure: 750 ng of total RNA was used for cDNA synthesis, followed by an amplification/labeling step (in vitro transcription) to synthesize biotin-labeled cRNA using the Illumina TotalPrep RNA Amplification kit (Ambion, Inc., Austin, TX). cRNA concentrations were determined using a spectrophotometer (Nanodrop, ND-1000)."	"Biotin-labeled cRNA samples for hybridization were prepared according to Illumina's recommended sample labeling procedure: 750 ng of total RNA was used for cDNA synthesis, followed by an amplification/labeling step (in vitro transcription) to synthesize biotin-labeled cRNA using the Illumina TotalPrep RNA Amplification kit (Ambion, Inc., Austin, TX). cRNA concentrations were determined using a spectrophotometer (Nanodrop, ND-1000)."	"Biotin-labeled cRNA samples for hybridization were prepared according to Illumina's recommended sample labeling procedure: 750 ng of total RNA was used for cDNA synthesis, followed by an amplification/labeling step (in v